       physically-correct t0 stock threshold (tau_min + one legal lot, was
       tau* + median campaign length -- 5.1x too high on PCR).
       BOTH REVERTED IN v13 -- see below.
  v13  OVERFITTING CORRECTION. v12's two flags were adopted on a July-only
       A/B. Re-measured on BOTH months on the in-month basis:

         PLANNER_WARM_PRESS=1        Jul PCR +0.6   Aug PCR -0.5, L11 -1
         PLANNER_T0_STOCK_BASIS=lot  Jul TBR +0.1   Aug TBR -0.7, L11 -2

       Both now default OFF/star. Cost July 0.6 pt PCR that was never real
       generalisation; recovered August TBR 0.7 pt and 2 invariants on a pack
       that ships to the plant.

       NOT a data artefact: August resolves MORE presses than July for the
       warm-press bridge (PCR 86 % vs 79 %). The effect is month-dependent.

       The two months differ in exactly the ways that matter -- July's demand
       IS the plant's own July output (100 % achievable, no partition, 48 PCR
       GTs); August is a forward order book, arithmetically infeasible by
       ~3.2 pt, partitioned, 73 PCR GTs, tighter TBR allowable matrix. A flag
       tuned on July is tuned on the easy month.

       new: scripts/ab_both_months.py  runs any candidate flag against current
       defaults on both months and exits REJECT unless NON-NEGATIVE ON BOTH,
       per plant, 0.05 pt tolerance. "Net positive across the two" is NOT
       sufficient: a +0.6/-0.5 flag is noise with a sign, and shipping it
       degrades a real pack to flatter a backtest.

